{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_91","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nSix blockers remain: mandatory-human overlay bypass, incomplete receipt verification, incorrect historical classification, two ADR handling gaps, and inconsistent terminal-state projections. Two low-severity CLI issues are follow-ups.\n\nValidation: root `pose validate --strict` passed 213/213 checks. The separate module run timed out on its unit step; the successful root run subsequently covered that module. Focused policy tests, CLI publication testing under `-race`, and `go vet` passed. The repository remains unchanged.\n\nApplied the `pose-review` skill and Go, security, documentation-style, delivery-evidence, and knowledge-governance rules. No assessment writers or attestation commands were run.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F1\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go\",\n      \"line\": 305,\n      \"summary\": \"Mandatory-human protection ignores selected overlays. mandatoryHumanReview examines only reviewer_independence and the base profile, whereas ReviewPlan composes overlay independence at review_plan.go:350. With never, a matching mandatory-human overlay and no recorded aggregate review, the gate grants an exemption before that effective obligation is enforced. Resolve the effective human requirement, including protected baseline obligations, before granting an exemption.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F2\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go\",\n      \"line\": 359,\n      \"summary\": \"Receipt verification checks only canonical member identities and never verifies SubjectDigest or the closed semantic inputs. After an exempt close, changing a milestone exit gate while retaining its member names leaves the receipt standing; repeated close returns before rerunning roadmapGate. Conversely, this function evaluates the current policy, so changing never to when-justified can invalidate an unchanged historical receipt through newly inspected unresolved ADR inputs. Verify semantic integrity under the recorded closeout contract while preserving later policy independence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F3\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go\",\n      \"line\": 415,\n      \"summary\": \"Historical classification is inferred from parent roadmap status and absent receipt/intent rather than positive prior terminal evidence. Marking an adopted roadmap done without an intent re-enables legacy singleton inheritance despite always. In the opposite direction, a milestone with its own valid sealed approval before adoption is reopened when its parent roadmap remains active, because it now owes a receipt. Preserve positively established historical closures without treating status alone as proof of pre-adoption closure.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F4\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go\",\n      \"line\": 195,\n      \"summary\": \"A when-justified roadmap with at most one distinct member returns Known=true and Required=false before resolving any ADR associations. An explicit missing or malformed adrs declaration, or an unreadable ADR inventory, therefore grants an exemption. The spec permits skipping ADR inventory for never and always, but requires unknown association inputs to block when-justified exemptions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F5\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\",\n      \"line\": 140,\n      \"summary\": \"The ADR inventory can silently omit unresolved inputs. README.md is skipped even when explicitly associated, so its contents, size and backward declaration are never validated. At line 143, regularADR failures are also ignored unless a forward association already identified that filename; an unreadable or dangling candidate that might contain a backlink consequently becomes absence. Unknown inventory entries must produce diagnostics rather than establish an exemption.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F6\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go\",\n      \"line\": 478,\n      \"summary\": \"Doctor and reached/attention projections bypass terminal verification. Doctor skips every done roadmap and every scope with any parseable receipt, including an interrupted done roadmap still owing review or a receipt whose recorded review no longer stands. ReachedMilestones, roadmapReachedApartFrom and milestoneReachedObligations likewise use receipt presence without checking its standing. A later rejection or composition change can make closeout-check nonterminal while doctor reports no review owed and attention hides the scope. These readers must project the same applicable gate.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F7\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/adopt.go\",\n      \"line\": 101,\n      \"summary\": \"The --request branch returns before validating closeoutPairGiven. A command combining --request with either new closeout flag silently ignores the flags, even for another capability or an incomplete pair, instead of rejecting the combination.\",\n      \"action\": \"Reject closeout policy flags with --request and --list before entering their early-return branches; add CLI argument coverage.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-13\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F8\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/adopt.go\",\n      \"line\": 310,\n      \"summary\": \"Fresh installation advertises pose adopt closeout-review-policy --off --apply as the way to turn this capability off, although its RetireRefusal deliberately rejects that command. The installation output gives an unusable remediation instruction.\",\n      \"action\": \"Render the closeout capability's supported pair-change command instead of the generic --off instruction.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-13\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F1\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_review_policy.go:305 protects policy/base-profile human requirements, but selected overlay requirements remain bypassable; F1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F2\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go:2457 requires state.Terminal for receipt-backed repeated close; TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRepeatedCloseVerifiesTheTerminalContract passed in the focused run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F3\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go:2476 uses CloseoutRecoveryDecision and refuses required-unapproved or recorded-unapproved recovery.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F4\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_review_policy.go:367 now compares canonical members and closeout_receipt.go:114 rejects always/not-required, but semantic receipt integrity remains incomplete; F2.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F5\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go:2117 records an intent before status publication, fixing engine-interruption handling. Historical classification still lacks positive historical proof; F3.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F6\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go:1526 evaluates the adopted gate before enabled/cutoff shortcuts; focused protection tests passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F7\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/federated_acceptance.go:701 supplies receipt-bound proof after terminal source verification; TestCloseoutReviewPolicyFederatedReceiptProof passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F8\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go:2530 rechecks CurrentCloseoutDecision before publication, using the same protected producer as preflight.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F9\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go:2503 rejects non-lifecycle blockers; verifyCloseoutPublication rechecks decision, members, associations and state.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F10\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go:265 follows transferred members through the resolver to final identity and refuses resolution without a bound resolver.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F11\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go:149 validates ordinary associated ADRs, but README and unresolved inventory entries still escape complete validation; F5.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F12\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go:407 propagates gate errors; TestCloseoutReviewPolicyReceiptIntegrity passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F13\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/surface_check.go:406 normalizes typed local spec members; TestCloseoutReviewPolicyTypedLocalMemberCloses passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F14\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go:353 requires Known for exemption, but the small-roadmap branch incorrectly establishes Known without resolving associations; F4.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F15\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go:504 requires a fresh approval for scopes it examines, but earlier status/receipt shortcuts hide nonterminal scopes; F6.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed R1-R7, D1-D2, the accepted ADR, changed implementation/tests/schemas/docs/templates, adoption and schema transitions, canonical members, ADR inventory, receipts and intents, CLI close/recovery/repetition, closeout-check, review-check, review verification, review-plan, attention/obligations, reached/nextCloses, roadmap check, MCP state, federated acceptance and doctor. Checked the adversarial corpus inventory: its closeout-plan judgment case does not cover the overlay, history-classification or receipt semantic-drift bypasses reported here. Ran artifact-check, surface-check, suggest review, focused policy tests, CLI publication testing under race detection, go vet, root validation and module validation. Root validation passed 213/213; the separate module run had 209 passes and a 600-second unit timeout. Final git status was clean. No repository changes or attestation were made.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified authority at the requested head and distinguished sealed evidence, independently executed checks and code-derived findings. Historical closure, complete ADR absence and effective human requirements are not assumed proven merely by status, receipt presence or base-profile inspection. The module timeout is disclosed separately from the successful root run. Only F7/F8 are accepted low-severity follow-ups.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected existing write guards, intent-before-status ordering, ExpectAbsent receipt publication and protected rechecks. The focused CLI publication test passed under -race; its pose-package invocation had no matching test. No new goroutine lifecycle was introduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"F3\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Schema migration is explicit, but historical aggregate-state compatibility is not preserved correctly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"F4\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Unresolved association inputs can be returned as a known exemption.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"F6\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Doctor, reached and attention do not consistently consume the terminal gate used by closeout state.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"F6\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The diagnostic projection can report no review owed while authoritative closeout verification is nonterminal.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"F3\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Existing sealed milestone closures under active roadmaps can reopen, while status-only history can weaken adopted always.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"F2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A receipt can survive semantic changes that its original close never judged.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-a8489a97539b30e7\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1 separates aggregate review cost from mandatory explicit close; D2 supplies explicit adoption, canonical association inputs and a persistent receipt. A common domain evaluator directly addresses inconsistent thresholds across transports. The implementation defects are failures to complete those selected boundaries, rather than evidence against the accepted decision.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-607ff681\",\n          \"basis\": \"D2\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The roadmap template adds the planned flat adrs association syntax needed by R3.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-ec2d86f4\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The new accepted ADR records the policy semantics, deterministic thresholds, explicit close and historical compatibility required by R1.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"F8\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The manuals/templates describe the intended pair and receipt contract, but installation output recommends an unsupported rollback command.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"F6\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Operators can lose the obligation and next-action signal for a scope whose receipt or review no longer stands.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"F1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R5's non-waivable authority protection is incomplete; F2-F6 additionally leave R3, R4, R6 and R7 unsatisfied despite passing registered checks.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-a8489a97539b30e7\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The feature-owned changes implement the planned policy pair, evaluator, associations, receipt, adoption/setup, projections and distributed documentation. No unrelated feature expansion is needed to address the findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"F1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"An aggregate exemption can bypass a selected mandatory-human authority requirement. Path containment and immutable publication alone do not repair that authority gap.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-a8489a97539b30e7\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The pair of enums, existing adopt/setup surface, one evaluator and separate receipt are proportionate to the three requested modes and explicit-close requirement. A boolean cannot express when-justified, and an ephemeral exemption cannot establish explicit closure. Avoiding global ADR identities and remote backlink discovery limits speculative scope. A future requirement for remote association discovery would invalidate the present local-inventory boundary and require another design decision.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed; exit 0. Output included artifact.claims=39, artifact.observed=54 and artifact.findings=926, with warnings. Its attribution query reported cs-265abd4131d5 and head e94ae458 rather than the sealed brief's change set; this command result is not treated as proof that those ranges are identical.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-a8489a97539b30e7\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Used the sealed structural assessment and independently mapped both listed deltas to D1/D2. Did not rerun an assessment writer.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Discovery persists assessment/state artifacts. The review boundary forbids those writes; component scope was established from the sealed plan and source.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Did not run the assessment writer. Inspected CLI/MCP/federation consumers directly and used sealed integration evidence plus the successful root validation; F6 records a remaining integration divergence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Did not run the assessment writer inside the sealed checkout. Reviewed the changed sources and recorded concrete defects here without staging repository feedback or follow-up artifacts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion verification depends on the review attestation, which this independent run is explicitly forbidden to record.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The review's completion gate cannot establish this review's approval before POSE records its verified conclusion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed successfully; selected backend-go, security and documentation-style, with review workflow and implementation validation evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed pose surface-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict; exit 0, surface.targets=1, surface.results=213, surface.findings=0. Composition evidence: integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration. Reachability evidence: reachability:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-reachability. Passing composition does not resolve the reported semantic defects.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed pose validate --strict; exit 0, 213 step(s), 213 pass, Result: SUCCESS. The run included pose-mcp build, unit and registered integrations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp: 209 passes and one unit-step timeout after 600 seconds, exit 1. The subsequent successful root validation covered the same module, including its unit step and all required checks. This passed disposition rests on that successful module coverage and the sealed integration evidence, not on misclassifying the timed-out invocation.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
